atus/2116996709192495255"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-01T20:34:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116992174831075591"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A weekly dispatch exploring the latest news in math and AI…", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/updates/transf…", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/updates/transformation/#168483", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114851031775649792/ZLGRGsf1?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114851031775649792/ZLGRGsf1?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "Transformation | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/updates/transformation/#168483", "url": "https://t.co/itCgrklLAt"}]}, "id": "2116992174831075591", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 8546, "like_count": 55, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "On October 26, OpenAI announced that an advanced AI model had solved three major problems. Their claims: a proof of the local smoothing conjecture, a disproof of the exponential time hypothesis, and a proof that quantum field theories are consistent. https://t.co/itCgrklLAt", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2116992174831075591"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-01T20:12:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116986642141511955"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "2326120952", "start": 15, "username": "ScienceAdvances"}], "urls": [{"description": "Coral bleaching, the temperature-induced loss of dinoflagellate symbionts, is a major driver of global coral reef decline. Although corals can regain symbionts through repopulation of residual symbionts or via environmental acquisition, these processes ...", "display_url": "scim.ag/4s40Tt3", "end": 209, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4s40Tt3", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116986690967388160/2gYFfm8K?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116986690967388160/2gYFfm8K?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 186, "status": 200, "title": "Rapid coral bleaching recovery via symbiont transfer from healthy corals", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aeh1580?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_medium=ownedSocial&utm_source=twitter", "url": "https://t.co/xennKZbdW0"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/9fPtZvo8kL", "end": 233, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116986642141511955/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116986638903427072", "start": 210, "url": "https://t.co/9fPtZvo8kL"}]}, "id": "2116986642141511955", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 85, "impression_count": 61377, "like_count": 1012, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 169}, "text": "Researchers in @ScienceAdvances have demonstrated that brief physical contact between healthy and bleached coral can restore algae to the bleached coral, leading to their full recovery. https://t.co/xennKZbdW0 https://t.co/9fPtZvo8kL", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116986642141511955"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-01T19:45:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116979845510889633"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "They visited for what they thought were obvious urgent care issues — coughs, congestion, flu — and were shocked to get bills for ER care instead, totaling thousands of dollars. ", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/10/30/hyb…", "end": 180, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/30/hybrid-er-urgent-care-clinics-hidden-billing-complaints-intuitive-health/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116100377187639296/teGHtEYA?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116100377187639296/teGHtEYA?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 157, "status": 200, "title": "How a simple UTI turns into a $1,756 bill", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/30/hybrid-er-urgent-care-clinics-hidden-billing-complaints-intuitive-health/", "url": "https://t.co/5p0P2XD8c1"}]}, "id": "2116979845510889633", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 4348, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Patients at hybrid urgent care clinics report surprise ER bills. STAT looks at the growing business of hybrid medical hubs like those from Intuitive Health. https://t.co/5p0P2XD8c1", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2116979845510889633"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-01T18:33:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116961777166549260"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Political campaigns can do more than raise your blood pressure. Studies link election stress to irregular heartbeats and an increase in heart attacks.", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/10/30/ele…", "end": 88, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/30/election-stress-heart-attack-risk/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116185006552891392/Ra6A7KSC?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116185006552891392/Ra6A7KSC?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 65, "status": 200, "title": "How Election Day can affect your heart", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/30/election-stress-heart-attack-risk/", "url": "https://t.co/acYgln7Ili"}]}, "id": "2116961777166549260", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2270, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "‘Your political party doesn’t matter to your heart; stress does’ https://t.co/acYgln7Ili", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2116961777166549260"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-01T18:26:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116959962215719208"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - Faulty neurons can contribute to various neurological conditions, but researchers have uncovered a system that might clean them up.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/4A5vc5u", "end": 163, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/4A5vc5u", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116959970272919553/uAfTC-lU?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116959970272919553/uAfTC-lU?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 140, "status": 200, "title": "The brain liquidates billions of mutant neurons around the time we’re born", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03444-x?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64276659&error=cookies_not_supported&code=e3bbb8ee-b6ae-49dc-aad8-7e68f309353b", "url": "https://t.co/GzN0tl79Ii"}]}, "id": "2116959962215719208", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 42, "impression_count": 21011, "like_count": 117, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 54}, "text": "Around the time of birth, the developing human brain mysteriously tidies up by purging itself of a vast number of mutation-riddled neurons\n\nhttps://t.co/GzN0tl79Ii", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2116959962215719208"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-01T17:49:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116950666073583685"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 153, "id": "17089636", "start": 137, "username": "NewsfromScience"}], "urls": [{"description": "Jumping spiders enter a REM-like state, darting their eyes and twitching their legs. What’s happening beyond that remains unclear", "display_url": "scim.ag/4sugguV", "end": 136, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4sugguV", "images": [{"height": 804, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114798913622286337/BY7yNCNU?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1216}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114798913622286337/BY7yNCNU?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 113, "status": 200, "title": "These spiders go to sleep at night, a new study reveals. But do they dream?", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/content/article/these-spiders-go-sleep-night-new-study-reveals-do-they-dream?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=ownedSocial", "url": "https://t.co/VV5qjRkMIk"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/7u00N3yZo4", "end": 177, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116950666073583685/video/1", "media_key": "13_2116950652534325248", "start": 154, "url": "https://t.co/7u00N3yZo4"}]}, "id": "2116950666073583685", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 84, "impression_count": 49100, "like_count": 513, "quote_count": 19, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 98}, "text": "Jumping spiders actually fall asleep, even entering a REM-like state in which they may be dreaming.\n\nLearn more: https://t.co/VV5qjRkMIk @NewsfromScience https://t.co/7u00N3yZo4", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116950666073583685"}, {"author_id": "15134240", "created_at": "2026-11-01T17:11:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116941097058394486"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/DLcQumU0G8", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2116941097058394486/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116941093426069505", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/DLcQumU0G8"}]}, "id": "2116941097058394486", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 8220, "like_count": 36, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 16}, "text": "Researchers funded by NIH found that a combination of genetic and biomarker testing might be better at detecting dementia risk than either one alone. \n\nThe findings could help doctors better predict dementia risk and estimate the timing of future symptoms. \n\nLearn more: https://t.co/DLcQumU0G8", "url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2116941097058394486"}